Package: presence
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: ProdBytes <julio@nu01.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Section: video
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/prodbytes/presence
Depends: adduser, cage, xwayland, chromium | chromium-browser, libc6 (>= 2.35), libgcc-s1, libstdc++6, libglib2.0-0 (>= 2.72), libgtk-3-0, libepoxy0, libfontconfig1, libegl1, libgles2
Recommends: libcamera-v4l2
Description: Presence camera kiosk
 Turns the machine (a Raspberry Pi with Raspberry Pi OS Lite, 64-bit) into
 a Presence camera: at boot, presence-kiosk.service runs Presence full
 screen on tty1 under the cage Wayland compositor, as the presence system
 user, and restarts it whenever it stops. By default it shows the Presence
 web app in Chromium, which records from a USB webcam; the native Linux
 app is installed in /opt/presence/bundle (the presence command).
 .
 Settings: /etc/default/presence. Turn the kiosk on or off with
 sudo presence-kiosk enable|disable.
